<title>POLAND: Polish trade gap grows to $7.78 bln in Jan-Jun.</title>
<headline>Polish trade gap grows to $7.78 bln in Jan-Jun.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's registered trade gap in the first six months of 1997 amounted to $7.78 billion, up from $5.53 billion the same period of 1996, the Central Statistical Office said (GUS).  </p>
<p> POLISH TRADE (MLN USD)     JAN-JUN 97	   JAN-JUN 96</p>
<p> Trade balance		   -7,778		   -5,532</p>
<p> exports			   12,221			N.A.</p>
<p> imports			   19,999			N.A.</p>
<p> TRADE WITH EU		  JAN-JUN 97	   JAN-JUN 96</p>
<p> Trade balance		  -14,766		   -4,780</p>
<p> exports				N.A.		     N.A.</p>
<p> imports				N.A.		     N.A.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
